# Turn off the camera half of the SoC.
#
# rv1106_defconfig is written for an IP camera, so it pulls in the whole V4L2
# subsystem, the Rockchip ISP and CIF drivers, the RGA blitter, the video
# encoder, the audio codec -- and, once olddefconfig fills in the defaults, the
# entire DVB tuner catalogue. That is ~130 modules and a large chunk of the
# build for hardware this image does not use, on a board whose devicetree
# leaves all of it disabled anyway.
#
# It also fixes a build failure: Rockchip's rga3 driver calls
# __pte_offset_map_lock, which 6.6 does not export, so ROCKCHIP_MULTI_RGA=m
# cannot pass modpost.
#
# Merged after glibc-distro.config, so these wins are final. If you do want the
# camera, delete this file -- everything else in the tree stays valid.

# CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MULTI_RGA is not set
# CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_DVBM is not set
# CONFIG_SOUND is not set
